    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\tGlobal variables section is included in the &ldquo;main&rdquo; activation record of the program. All activation record makes access link to the &ldquo;main&rdquo; to access the global variables.</p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "type": "NAT",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>\n\tA grammar that has not any epsilon productions and also free from unit productions. The maximum number of reduce moves that can be taken during bottom up evaluation of 25 token string by bottom up parsers is ________.</p>",
   "options": [],
   "answer": null,
   "natRange": [
    49,
    49
   ],
   "answerText": "49",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t49<br />\n\tMaximum number of reduce moves for <em>n</em> token = 2<em>n</em> &ndash; 1<br />\n\tSo, for 25 tokens = 2 &times; 25 &ndash; 1 = 49</p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Handle is a sub-string that matches right side of production whose reduction to non-terminal on left sides of production represents one step along the reverse of left-most derivation.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Viable prefixes of grammar G are those prefixes of right sentential form that appears on stack of shift reduce parsing.<br />\n\tWhich of the following is true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>\n\tNeither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; Handle is a sub-string that matches right side of production whose reduction to non-terminal on left hand side of production represents one step along the reverse of right-most derivation.<br />\n\t&bull; Viable prefixes are those prefixes of right sentential form that can appear on the stack of a shift reduce parser.</p>"
  },
  {
